Reincarnation has a really serious problem with finding a complex enough
structure in which to preserve the self between bodies, not to mention the
mechanism for inserting the self into a new body and not to mention the
mind body duality problems the entire subject brings up. 

 The only possible mechanism for preservation of the self after death that
I have come across is a many universes interpretation of reality with all
of the universes "overlapped" and with a physical mechanism for transfer of
complex information between them - A formidable set of conditions!   This
scenario would have the Self existing in a very large number of bodies
simultaneously.  Each one would be similar to a cell in a larger body. 
When one dies there is loss of cell self but not of essential Self. 
Presumably the Self could inhabit new bodies as they became available.  

Even if true this would not negate the individual cells efforts at
continuity.  After all we would be in some trouble if all of the cells in
our own bodies did not so strive.  Such a scenario would however take off
some of the pressure to survive death.  Until such a thing is proved
however, make mine immortality.

